Here is what I found. All paths are absolute.

## 1. Owner creation

**Service (the create logic): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`**

The `createOwner` method (lines 267-295) is where an Owner is built up and persisted. Note the last two lines: it saves, then calls the audit logger.

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public String createOwner(Owner owner, boolean sharesHousehold) throws DataAccessException {
    if (DisposableEmailDomains.isDisposable(owner.getEmail())) {
        throw new DisposableEmailDomainException(owner.getEmail());
    }
    owner.setHouseholdId(HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()));
    rejectIdentityCollision(owner);
    List<Owner> householdMembers = findHouseholdMembers(owner);
    long ownersInCity = ownerRepository.countByCity(owner.getCity());
    if (ownersInCity >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY) {
        throw new CityCapacityExceededException(owner.getCity(), MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY);
    }
    LocalDate effectiveDate = owner.getRegistrationDate() == null ? LocalDate.now() : owner.getRegistrationDate();
    owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay(effectiveDate));
    long ownersOnDate = ownerRepository.countByRegistrationDate(owner.getRegistrationDate());
    if (ownersOnDate >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY) {
        throw new DailyOwnerLimitExceededException(owner.getRegistrationDate(), MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY);
    }
    owner.setBulkSignupWarning(ownersOnDate > BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD);
    flagPossibleDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold);
    owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner));
    owner.setHouseholdSize(householdMembers.size() + 1);
    owner.setMembershipLevel(OwnerMembership.cappedLevel(owner, householdMembers));
    owner.setCustomerCode(assignCustomerCode(owner));
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
    ownerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(owner);       // <-- audit hook
    return owner.getHouseholdId();
}
```

`assignCustomerCode` (326-334) builds the `customerCode`; `OwnerAuditLogger` is injected via the constructor (field at line 61, wired at line 70/77). Interface declaration: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` line 59 (`String createOwner(Owner owner, boolean sharesHousehold)`).

**Controller (the ONE create endpoint, `POST /api/owners`): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**, method `addOwner` (lines 118-135). It maps the DTO to an `Owner`, calls `clinicService.createOwner(owner, sharesHousehold)`, records the idempotency key, and returns 201 with a `Location` header. The V2 controller (`.../v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java`) only has list/paging, no create.

## 2. Auditing — the exact current form of the audit line emission

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/audit/OwnerAuditLogger.java`** — the entire audit mechanism. It logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `"AUDIT"`.

```java
@Component
public class OwnerAuditLogger {

    private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");

    public void ownerCreated(Owner owner) {
        AUDIT.info(
            "Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}",
            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
            membershipLevel(owner), membershipNumber(owner));
    }

    private static int membershipLevel(Owner owner) {
        return OwnerMembership.level(owner);
    }

    private static String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {
        return MembershipNumberFormatter.format(owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());
    }
}
```

So today exactly one audit line is emitted per owner creation, at INFO level, on logger `AUDIT`, in the human-readable form:
`Owner created: id=… customerCode=… registrationDate=… membershipLevel=… membershipNumber=…`

There is currently **no** structured `OWNER_CREATED` event and **no** `memberId`/`ownerId`-keyed event — only this single formatted line.

Logger config: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/logback.xml` (Logback; console appender, root at INFO, so the `AUDIT` logger inherits INFO — the audit line is emitted). There is no separate `AUDIT` logger declared, so it uses the root appender.

## 3. References to customerCode / membershipLevel / memberId / ownerId

- **customerCode**: model field + getter/setter in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (field line 73, getter 182, setter 186). Generated by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CustomerCodeGenerator.java` (`format`, `deduplicate`, `region`). Assigned in `ClinicServiceImpl.assignCustomerCode` (326-334). Region resolution in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/LocalityResolver.java`. Also referenced in repositories (`OwnerRepository`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `SpringDataOwnerRepository` — `findByCustomerCodeStartingWith`) and `OwnerMapper`.
- **membershipLevel**: model field line 85 (getter 214, setter 218). Derived in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/OwnerMembership.java` (`naturalLevel`, `level`, `cappedLevel`) which uses `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/MembershipLevelFormatter.java`. Set in `createOwner` line 290. Membership *number* comes from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/MembershipNumberFormatter.java`.
- **ownerId**: used throughout `OwnerRestControllerV1` as the path variable / method parameter name (getOwner, updateOwner, deleteOwner, addPetToOwner, etc.). It is **not** currently emitted in the audit line (the audit line uses `id=`). Also `IdempotencyKeyRegistry.ownerIdFor(...)`.
- **memberId**: appears **only** in a comment in the acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.java` line 10) describing a future checkpoint where the event's identifier "switched to the memberId." No production code uses it yet.

## 4. Tests related to owner creation and audit

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — the only assertion test. Its single test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` (lines 13-22) creates an owner, then asserts, via `AuditLogCapture`, that one `AUDIT` line contains all of `"OWNER_CREATED"`, the owner id, and the returned `customerCode`:

```java
try (AuditLogCapture audit = new AuditLogCapture()) {
    int id = createOwnerOk(knownOwner("Sydney"));
    JsonNode r = fetchOwner(id);
    assertTrue(audit.anyContains("OWNER_CREATED", String.valueOf(id),
            r.get("customerCode").asText()));
}
```

Important: this test expects an `"OWNER_CREATED"` marker containing the id and customerCode. The current `OwnerAuditLogger` emits `"Owner created: id=… customerCode=…"` — it does **not** contain the literal `OWNER_CREATED`, so this assertion would currently fail. The class-level Javadoc (lines 7-10) states the intended behavior: besides the human-readable audit line, emit a structured event via `AUDIT` `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}`, carrying the owner id AND the current primary identifier (customerCode now, memberId later).

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java`** — test utility that attaches a Logback `ListAppender` to the `AUDIT` logger and exposes `messages()`, `anyContains(...)`, `anyAtLevel(level, ...)`, `count()`.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — black-box base class: `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(username="acceptance-admin", roles={"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`. Provides `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`/`createOwnerWithKey`, `fetchOwner`, `knownOwner(city)`, unique-field generators, pinned reference tables (CITY_REGION, REGION_POSTCODES, HOLIDAYS), and expectation helpers (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`, `toBusinessDay`). All tests exercise only `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`.

## Build system and running tests

- **Build system: Maven** (single module). `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`, artifact `spring-petclinic-rest`, parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`. Wrapper present: `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (and `mvnw.cmd`), `.mvn/`. Test stack: `spring-boot-starter-test`, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test`, `spring-boot-starter-security-test`, `mockito-core`, and `tools.jackson` (Jackson 3). No Gradle files exist.
- **Run all tests:** `./mvnw test` (from `/home/daniel/sandbox`). Full verify/build: `./mvnw clean install` or `./mvnw verify`.
- **Run just the acceptance test:** `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.
- **Run the app:** `./mvnw spring-boot:run` (per readme.md line 25). Test resources: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/resources/application.properties`.

Note (not asked, but load-bearing): to make `AcceptanceTest` pass, the audit emission in `OwnerAuditLogger.ownerCreated` would need to additionally emit an `AUDIT` event containing the literal `OWNER_CREATED` plus the owner id and `customerCode`; the current single line does not include that marker.

